response:
 To find the length of the shadow cast by the 15-foot flagpole, we can use the concept of similar triangles constructed using the woman and the flagpole. The triangle of the woman's height and shadow side are similar to the triangle of the flagpole's 15-feet height and shadow. So, divide the flagpole's length by the height of the woman and multiply the quantity of that by the 6-foot shadow distance. We get:

{eq}\begin{align}

\frac{15\text{ feet}}{5.0\text{ feet}} = \frac{x}{6.0\text{ ft}}

\end{align}

{/eq}

or

{eq}\begin{align}

x=18\text{ feet}

\end{align}

{/eq}

Therefore, the length of the shadow of the flagpole is 18 feet.

