How can we find the reverse of an integer without using any string methods in C#? To reverse an integer in C# without using string methods, we can use the modulus operator (%) and division by 10. Here's a C# code snippet that demonstrates this approach:

```csharp
public int Reverse(int x)
{
    int r = 0;
    while(x != 0)
    {
        //modulus will give the least digit left, hence we add it to the result
        //by adding it to (r % 10). Also, to remove the left digit we divide r with 10.
        r = r * 10 + x % 10;
        x /= 10;
    }
    return r;
}
```

